{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5FQb2XKDzHzDfsKHkYvYY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Flight Deck\n2\t\n3\tA local, single-user console for working on many projects at once: pick a project,\n4\ttalk to Claude about it, review what changed, commit. One window instead of twenty\n5\tVS Code windows.\n6\t\n7\tNot deployed. Not multi-user. No auth. Runs on `localhost` on one machine.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Why this exists\n12\t\n13\tVS Code is good at one project at a time. With ~20 repos under `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio`,\n14\tthe cost is not the editing — it is the *switching*: a window per project, a chat per\n15\twindow, and no memory of what the last conversation about that repo was.\n16\t\n17\tFlight Deck keeps the projects, their conversations, and their diffs in one place.\n18\t\n19\t**Explicit non-goal:** replacing VS Code. Editing still happens in the editor (or by\n20\tthe agent). Flight Deck is a control surface — chat, review, commit.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## Why there is a server at all\n25\t\n26\tThere is no separate backend service. There is one app with two halves:\n27\t\n28\t- **Browser half** — React. Renders everything.\n29\t- **Node half** — Fastify. Does the things a browser physically cannot: spawn `claude`,\n30\t  run `git`, read `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio`, open a PTY.\n31\t\n32\tNo database, no deploy target, no port to expose. In dev it is two processes (Vite +\n33\tFastify); in \"production\" the built static files are served by Fastify itself, so\n34\trunning Flight Deck is one command and a `localhost` tab.\n35\t\n36\tThe only alternative shape is Electron/Tauri — the same Node half wrapped in a desktop\n37\twindow. That is what the previous attempt was, and its native-module rebuild pain is\n38\texactly what this avoids.\n39\t\n40\t---\n41\t\n42\t## Decisions (locked)\n43\t\n44\t| Decision | Choice | Why |\n45\t|---|---|---|\n46\t| Stack | **Vite + React + Fastify**, one repo | The terminal needs WebSockets, which App Router route handlers cannot do without a custom server. Nothing here benefits from SSR or server components. |\n47\t| Project discovery | **Manual list** | You add each project by folder. Nothing appears unasked. The picker defaults to `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio` but can browse anywhere. |\n48\t| Default permission mode | **`acceptEdits`** | Edits apply without prompting; bash still asks. Overridable per chat. |\n49\t| Agent transport | **`claude` CLI, headless** | Runs on the existing Claude subscription (OAuth) — no API key, no per-token billing. |\n50\t| Git access | **`simple-git`** (wraps the real `git` binary) | `stash` / `fetch` / `pull` / `revert` / `reset` all work. `isomorphic-git` is pure JS and missing exactly those. |\n51\t| Chat rendering | **Collapsible tool cards** | Text streams as prose; each edit / bash / read is a card with the diff or output inside. This is what makes the agent's actions reviewable. |\n52\t| Terminal | **Plain shell per project**, Phase 3 | A normal shell opened in the project folder, fully isolated from the agent's process, so it can never affect chat or git. |\n53\t| Commits | **Never automatic** | The agent edits the working tree. A human reads the diff and commits. |\n54\t\n55\t---\n56\t\n57\t## The safety model (one rule)\n58\t\n59\tThe agent edits the working tree. **It never commits, never pushes, never switches\n60\tbranches.** You review the diff in the Changes tab and commit yourself.\n61\t\n62\tThat one rule replaces everything a heavier harness needs — no git worktrees, no\n63\t`agent/*` branches, no per-agent `npm ci`, no `.env` copying. The working tree is the\n64\tsandbox, `git diff` is the audit log, `git restore` is the undo.\n65\t\n66\tConsequences to respect:\n67\t\n68\t- Two chats in the same project share one working tree. Running them concurrently on\n69\t  the same files will interleave edits. The UI must show when a project already has a\n70\t  live chat.\n71\t- `bypassPermissions` stays a deliberate per-chat toggle, never a default.\n72\t- The Phase 3 terminal is *yours*. The agent never gets a PTY — it runs commands\n73\t  through its own Bash tool, and that output appears in the chat as a tool card.\n74\t\n75\t---\n76\t\n77\t## Architecture\n78\t\n79\t```\n80\tbrowser (React, Vite)\n81\t   |  SSE          (chat stream)\n82\t   |  WebSocket    (terminal bytes, Phase 3)\n83\t   |  fetch        (everything else)\n84\t   v\n85\tFastify (Node)\n86\t   |-- spawn: claude -p --output-format stream-json   (cwd = project path)\n87\t   |-- simple-git: status / diff / stage / commit / stash / fetch / pull\n88\t   +-- node-pty: one PTY per open terminal            (Phase 3)\n89\t   v\n90\tE:\\muhaz\\CStudio\\<project>       the real repo, real working tree\n91\t~/.flightdeck/state.json          projects + chats + session ids\n92\t```\n93\t\n94\t### Agent transport — verified against Claude Code 2.1.233\n95\t\n96\t```bash\n97\tclaude -p \\\n98\t  --output-format stream-json \\\n99\t  --input-format stream-json \\\n100\t  --include-partial-messages \\\n101\t  --session-id <uuid> \\\n102\t  --permission-mode acceptEdits\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\t- `cwd` of the spawned process **is** the project. That is the whole \"project scoping\".\n106\t- Emits JSON lines (text chunks, tool calls, tool results) which are forwarded to the\n107\t  browser over SSE and rendered as prose + tool cards.\n108\t- Multi-turn: keep the process alive and write JSON messages to stdin, or re-invoke\n109\t  with `--resume <sessionId>`.\n110\t- `--add-dir` for a project that legitimately spans folders (e.g. `com8_realty`).\n111\t- **Do not use `--bare`** — its own docs state OAuth is never read and an API key is\n112\t  required. The plain form is what keeps this on the subscription.\n113\t\n114\tKeep every process invocation inside `server/agent.ts`. If the Claude Agent SDK\n115\t(`@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`) turns out to authenticate with the subscription\n116\ttoo, swapping transport is then one file, not a rewrite.\n117\t\n118\t### Chats and sub-chats\n119\t\n120\tA chat *is* a session id. Nothing more.\n121\t\n122\t```\n123\tProject (com8_studio)\n124\t|-- Chat \"article schema\"        session 7f3a...  permissionMode: acceptEdits\n125\t|   +-- Sub-chat \"sanity side\"   session 91b2...  (parentChatId set)\n126\t+-- Chat \"perf pass\"             session c4d1...\n127\t```\n128\t\n129\tSub-chats are ordinary chats with a `parentChatId` — they exist for grouping in the\n130\tsidebar, not for any special agent behaviour. One-to-many rows either way, so the data\n131\tmodel carries them from day one even though the sidebar UI lands in Phase 3.\n132\t\n133\t### History replay\n134\t\n135\tReopening a chat must eventually show its past messages, not just resume silently.\n136\t\n137\tClaude Code already persists this, so Flight Deck stores no message history of its own.\n138\tTranscripts live under `~/.claude/projects/<encoded-cwd>/` as JSONL — one record per\n139\tevent, each with `type` (`user` / `assistant` / `attachment` / ...), a `message`\n140\t`{role, content}`, `uuid`, `timestamp`, and `cwd`. Encoded cwd example:\n141\t`E:\\muhaz\\CStudio\\com8-sanity` becomes `E--muhaz-CStudio-com8-sanity`.\n142\t\n143\tReplay = locate the file for `sessionId`, parse the JSONL, and render it through the\n144\tsame components the live stream uses. Confirm the exact main-transcript filename at\n145\timplementation time (a session directory can also contain `subagents/*.jsonl`).\n146\t\n147\tPhase 1 may resume without replay; Phase 2 renders it.\n148\t\n149\t### State\n150\t\n151\t`~/.flightdeck/state.json` — one file, written atomically (temp file + rename).\n152\t\n153\t```jsonc\n154\t{\n155\t  \"version\": 1,\n156\t  \"lastBrowsedDir\": \"E:\\\\muhaz\\\\CStudio\",   // add-project dialog starts here\n157\t  \"projects\": [\n158\t    {\n159\t      \"id\": \"com8_studio\",\n160\t      \"name\": \"Com8 Studio\",\n161\t      \"path\": \"E:\\\\muhaz\\\\CStudio\\\\com8_studio\",\n162\t      \"addedAt\": \"2026-08-18T00:00:00Z\",\n163\t      \"defaultPermissionMode\": \"acceptEdits\",\n164\t      \"verifyCommand\": \"npm run build\"      // optional, offered as a one-click check\n165\t    }\n166\t  ],\n167\t  \"chats\": [\n168\t    {\n169\t      \"id\": \"...\",\n170\t      \"projectId\": \"com8_studio\",\n171\t      \"parentChatId\": null,\n172\t      \"title\": \"article schema\",\n173\t      \"sessionId\": \"7f3a...\",               // the --session-id UUID\n174\t      \"permissionMode\": \"acceptEdits\",\n175\t      \"createdAt\": \"...\",\n176\t      \"lastMessageAt\": \"...\"\n177\t    }\n178\t  ]\n179\t}\n180\t```\n181\t\n182\t---\n183\t\n184\t## API surface\n185\t\n186\t| Route | Purpose |\n187\t|---|---|\n188\t| `GET /api/projects` | list projects from state |\n189\t| `POST /api/projects` | add one (validate: absolute path, exists, is a git repo) |\n190\t| `DELETE /api/projects/:id` | remove from the list (never touches the folder) |\n191\t| `GET /api/fs/browse?dir=` | folder listing for the add-project picker |\n192\t| `GET /api/chats?projectId=` | chats + sub-chats for a project |\n193\t| `POST /api/chats` | create a chat (mints a session UUID) |\n194\t| `GET /api/chats/:id/history` | replayed transcript for this chat's session |\n195\t| `POST /api/chat/:id/message` | **SSE** — send a prompt, stream the agent's output |\n196\t| `POST /api/chat/:id/abort` | kill the child process for this chat |\n197\t| `GET /api/git/status?projectId=` | staged / unstaged / untracked |\n198\t| `GET /api/git/diff?projectId=&file=&staged=` | unified diff for one file |\n199\t| `POST /api/git/stage` · `unstage` · `discard` | per file |\n200\t| `POST /api/git/commit` | message + optional file subset |\n201\t| `POST /api/git/stash` · `stash-pop` · `stash-list` | |\n202\t| `POST /api/git/fetch` · `pull` | |\n203\t| `GET /api/git/branches` · `log` | branch list, recent commits |\n204\t| `POST /api/git/checkout` | guarded — refuse when the tree is dirty |\n205\t| `WS /ws/terminal?projectId=` | PTY bytes in/out, plus a `resize` message (Phase 3) |\n206\t\n207\tEvery git and terminal route takes a `projectId` and resolves the path from state —\n208\t**never** a path supplied by the client. That is the one input-validation rule that\n209\treally matters here.\n210\t\n211\t---\n212\t\n213\t## UI\n214\t\n215\t```\n216\t+------------+------------------------------+---------------------+\n217\t| PROJECTS   |  CHAT                        |  CHANGES            |\n218\t|            |                              |                     |\n219\t| v Com8     |  +- chat: \"article schema\" -+|  M  src/app/page.tsx|\n220\t|   Studio   |  |  ...streamed prose...    ||  M  lib/schema.ts   |\n221\t|   |-article|  |  [+] Edit lib/schema.ts  ||  ?  docs/notes.md   |\n222\t|   +-perf   |  |  [+] Bash npm run build  ||                     |\n223\t| > Com8     |  +--------------------------+|  +- diff ----------+ |\n224\t|   Sanity   |  [ prompt input           ] |  | +  ...          | |\n225\t| + add      |  mode: acceptEdits v  [send] |  +----------------+ |\n226\t|            |                              |  [stage] [commit]   |\n227\t+------------+------------------------------+---------------------+\n228\t                         [ terminal ]  <- Phase 3, collapsible drawer\n229\t```\n230\t\n231\t- **Left** — projects, each expanding to its chats. `+ add` opens the folder picker\n232\t  (starts at `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio`, browses anywhere).\n233\t- **Middle** — the active chat. Prose streams inline; every tool call is a collapsible\n234\t  card (`[+] Edit lib/schema.ts`) holding the diff or command output. Permission-mode\n235\t  dropdown per chat: `acceptEdits` / `manual` / `bypassPermissions` / `plan`.\n236\t- **Right** — SCM for the active project: file list, diff, stage, commit, stash, fetch,\n237\t  pull.\n238\t- **Bottom** — Phase 3 terminal drawer, a plain shell in the project folder.\n239\t- A project with a live agent process shows a running indicator, so two chats don't\n240\t  quietly edit the same tree at once.\n241\t\n242\t---\n243\t\n244\t## Phases\n245\t\n246\t**Phase 1 — talk to a project** (the only phase that must exist to be useful)\n247\t\n248\t- Add / list / remove projects, folder picker defaulting to `CStudio`\n249\t- Create a chat, send a prompt, stream the response\n250\t- Prose + collapsible tool cards\n251\t- Per-chat permission mode, defaulting to `acceptEdits`\n252\t- Abort a running chat; resume a chat by session id\n253\t\n254\t**Phase 2 — see and commit what changed**\n255\t\n256\t- `status` file list: staged / unstaged / untracked\n257\t- Diff view (Monaco diff editor)\n258\t- Stage / unstage / discard; commit with a message\n259\t- Stash, stash pop\n260\t- History replay when reopening a chat\n261\t\n262\t**Phase 3 — terminal and the rest of source control**\n263\t\n264\t- Plain shell per project (`node-pty` + `xterm.js` over WebSocket), collapsible drawer\n265\t- Fetch, pull, branch list + guarded checkout, commit history\n266\t- Sub-chats in the sidebar\n267\t- Per-project `verifyCommand` with a one-click run and output panel\n268\t- Per-project `CLAUDE.md` editor\n269\t\n270\t---\n271\t\n272\t## Risks and things to get right\n273\t\n274\t- **Child-process lifecycle.** Map `chatId -> ChildProcess`. Kill on abort, on chat\n275\t  delete, and on server shutdown. An orphaned `claude` process holds a session and\n276\t  keeps working invisibly.\n277\t- **SSE plumbing.** Stream from Fastify with `Content-Type: text/event-stream` and no\n278\t  compression on that route. Verify with a slow response *before* building UI on it.\n279\t- **`node-pty` on Windows (Phase 3).** It installs from shipped prebuilds under plain\n280\t  Node — no compiler needed. Two known sharp edges: kill a PTY whose console has\n281\t  already exited and ConPTY's console-process enumeration can throw, and a browser\n282\t  refresh must dispose the PTY or processes leak. Own both explicitly.\n283\t- **Windows paths.** Backslashes in JSON, spaces in paths, `E:\\` vs `/e/` between Node\n284\t  and any shell call. Always pass argv arrays, never a concatenated command string.\n285\t- **Concurrent chats, one working tree.** Documented above; surface it in the UI rather\n286\t  than trying to solve it.\n287\t- **Long output.** Stream, don't buffer. Large diffs need virtualised lists or the\n288\t  Changes tab will jank on a big refactor.\n289\t\n290\t---\n291\t\n292\t## Deferred (deliberately not in v1)\n293\t\n294\t- Multi-agent anything — no orchestrator, no agent-to-agent messaging, no roster.\n295\t- Worktree isolation, per-agent branches.\n296\t- Any remote access, tunnel, or phone control.\n297\t- Scheduled or background runs. Nothing happens unless you press something.\n298\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38c7c23a-5f3f-48df-99be-0849fd9d3f50","uuid":"d7bc0e01-4ec6-43a8-a243-7d5e6f783c3c","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:17:52.631Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"e:\\muhaz\\flightdeck\\SPEC.md","content":"# Flight Deck\n\nA local, single-user console for working on many projects at once: pick a project,\ntalk to Claude about it, review what changed, commit. One window instead of twenty\nVS Code windows.\n\nNot deployed. Not multi-user. No auth. Runs on `localhost` on one machine.\n\n---\n\n## Why this exists\n\nVS Code is good at one project at a time. With ~20 repos under `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio`,\nthe cost is not the editing — it is the *switching*: a window per project, a chat per\nwindow, and no memory of what the last conversation about that repo was.\n\nFlight Deck keeps the projects, their conversations, and their diffs in one place.\n\n**Explicit non-goal:** replacing VS Code. Editing still happens in the editor (or by\nthe agent). Flight Deck is a control surface — chat, review, commit.\n\n---\n\n## Why there is a server at all\n\nThere is no separate backend service. There is one app with two halves:\n\n- **Browser half** — React. Renders everything.\n- **Node half** — Fastify. Does the things a browser physically cannot: spawn `claude`,\n  run `git`, read `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio`, open a PTY.\n\nNo database, no deploy target, no port to expose. In dev it is two processes (Vite +\nFastify); in \"production\" the built static files are served by Fastify itself, so\nrunning Flight Deck is one command and a `localhost` tab.\n\nThe only alternative shape is Electron/Tauri — the same Node half wrapped in a desktop\nwindow. That is what the previous attempt was, and its native-module rebuild pain is\nexactly what this avoids.\n\n---\n\n## Decisions (locked)\n\n| Decision | Choice | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stack | **Vite + React + Fastify**, one repo | The terminal needs WebSockets, which App Router route handlers cannot do without a custom server. Nothing here benefits from SSR or server components. |\n| Project discovery | **Manual list** | You add each project by folder. Nothing appears unasked. The picker defaults to `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio` but can browse anywhere. |\n| Default permission mode | **`acceptEdits`** | Edits apply without prompting; bash still asks. Overridable per chat. |\n| Agent transport | **`claude` CLI, headless** | Runs on the existing Claude subscription (OAuth) — no API key, no per-token billing. |\n| Git access | **`simple-git`** (wraps the real `git` binary) | `stash` / `fetch` / `pull` / `revert` / `reset` all work. `isomorphic-git` is pure JS and missing exactly those. |\n| Chat rendering | **Collapsible tool cards** | Text streams as prose; each edit / bash / read is a card with the diff or output inside. This is what makes the agent's actions reviewable. |\n| Terminal | **Plain shell per project**, Phase 3 | A normal shell opened in the project folder, fully isolated from the agent's process, so it can never affect chat or git. |\n| Commits | **Never automatic** | The agent edits the working tree. A human reads the diff and commits. |\n\n---\n\n## The safety model (one rule)\n\nThe agent edits the working tree. **It never commits, never pushes, never switches\nbranches.** You review the diff in the Changes tab and commit yourself.\n\nThat one rule replaces everything a heavier harness needs — no git worktrees, no\n`agent/*` branches, no per-agent `npm ci`, no `.env` copying. The working tree is the\nsandbox, `git diff` is the audit log, `git restore` is the undo.\n\nConsequences to respect:\n\n- Two chats in the same project share one working tree. Running them concurrently on\n  the same files will interleave edits. The UI must show when a project already has a\n  live chat.\n- `bypassPermissions` stays a deliberate per-chat toggle, never a default.\n- The Phase 3 terminal is *yours*. The agent never gets a PTY — it runs commands\n  through its own Bash tool, and that output appears in the chat as a tool card.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nbrowser (React, Vite)\n   |  SSE          (chat stream)\n   |  WebSocket    (terminal bytes, Phase 3)\n   |  fetch        (everything else)\n   v\nFastify (Node)\n   |-- spawn: claude -p --output-format stream-json   (cwd = project path)\n   |-- simple-git: status / diff / stage / commit / stash / fetch / pull\n   +-- node-pty: one PTY per open terminal            (Phase 3)\n   v\nE:\\muhaz\\CStudio\\<project>       the real repo, real working tree\n~/.flightdeck/state.json          projects + chats + session ids\n```\n\n### Agent transport — verified against Claude Code 2.1.233\n\n```bash\nclaude -p \\\n  --output-format stream-json \\\n  --input-format stream-json \\\n  --include-partial-messages \\\n  --session-id <uuid> \\\n  --permission-mode acceptEdits\n```\n\n- `cwd` of the spawned process **is** the project. That is the whole \"project scoping\".\n- Emits JSON lines (text chunks, tool calls, tool results) which are forwarded to the\n  browser over SSE and rendered as prose + tool cards.\n- Multi-turn: keep the process alive and write JSON messages to stdin, or re-invoke\n  with `--resume <sessionId>`.\n- `--add-dir` for a project that legitimately spans folders (e.g. `com8_realty`).\n- **Do not use `--bare`** — its own docs state OAuth is never read and an API key is\n  required. The plain form is what keeps this on the subscription.\n\nKeep every process invocation inside `server/agent.ts`. If the Claude Agent SDK\n(`@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`) turns out to authenticate with the subscription\ntoo, swapping transport is then one file, not a rewrite.\n\n### Chats and sub-chats\n\nA chat *is* a session id. Nothing more.\n\n```\nProject (com8_studio)\n|-- Chat \"article schema\"        session 7f3a...  permissionMode: acceptEdits\n|   +-- Sub-chat \"sanity side\"   session 91b2...  (parentChatId set)\n+-- Chat \"perf pass\"             session c4d1...\n```\n\nSub-chats are ordinary chats with a `parentChatId` — they exist for grouping in the\nsidebar, not for any special agent behaviour. One-to-many rows either way, so the data\nmodel carries them from day one even though the sidebar UI lands in Phase 3.\n\n### History replay\n\nReopening a chat must eventually show its past messages, not just resume silently.\n\nClaude Code already persists this, so Flight Deck stores no message history of its own.\nTranscripts live under `~/.claude/projects/<encoded-cwd>/` as JSONL — one record per\nevent, each with `type` (`user` / `assistant` / `attachment` / ...), a `message`\n`{role, content}`, `uuid`, `timestamp`, and `cwd`. Encoded cwd example:\n`E:\\muhaz\\CStudio\\com8-sanity` becomes `E--muhaz-CStudio-com8-sanity`.\n\nReplay = locate the file for `sessionId`, parse the JSONL, and render it through the\nsame components the live stream uses. Confirm the exact main-transcript filename at\nimplementation time (a session directory can also contain `subagents/*.jsonl`).\n\nPhase 1 may resume without replay; Phase 2 renders it.\n\n### State\n\n`~/.flightdeck/state.json` — one file, written atomically (temp file + rename).\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"lastBrowsedDir\": \"E:\\\\muhaz\\\\CStudio\",   // add-project dialog starts here\n  \"projects\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"com8_studio\",\n      \"name\": \"Com8 Studio\",\n      \"path\": \"E:\\\\muhaz\\\\CStudio\\\\com8_studio\",\n      \"addedAt\": \"2026-08-18T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"defaultPermissionMode\": \"acceptEdits\",\n      \"verifyCommand\": \"npm run build\"      // optional, offered as a one-click check\n    }\n  ],\n  \"chats\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"...\",\n      \"projectId\": \"com8_studio\",\n      \"parentChatId\": null,\n      \"title\": \"article schema\",\n      \"sessionId\": \"7f3a...\",               // the --session-id UUID\n      \"permissionMode\": \"acceptEdits\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"...\",\n      \"lastMessageAt\": \"...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## API surface\n\n| Route | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `GET /api/projects` | list projects from state |\n| `POST /api/projects` | add one (validate: absolute path, exists, is a git repo) |\n| `DELETE /api/projects/:id` | remove from the list (never touches the folder) |\n| `GET /api/fs/browse?dir=` | folder listing for the add-project picker |\n| `GET /api/chats?projectId=` | chats + sub-chats for a project |\n| `POST /api/chats` | create a chat (mints a session UUID) |\n| `GET /api/chats/:id/history` | replayed transcript for this chat's session |\n| `POST /api/chat/:id/message` | **SSE** — send a prompt, stream the agent's output |\n| `POST /api/chat/:id/abort` | kill the child process for this chat |\n| `GET /api/git/status?projectId=` | staged / unstaged / untracked |\n| `GET /api/git/diff?projectId=&file=&staged=` | unified diff for one file |\n| `POST /api/git/stage` · `unstage` · `discard` | per file |\n| `POST /api/git/commit` | message + optional file subset |\n| `POST /api/git/stash` · `stash-pop` · `stash-list` | |\n| `POST /api/git/fetch` · `pull` | |\n| `GET /api/git/branches` · `log` | branch list, recent commits |\n| `POST /api/git/checkout` | guarded — refuse when the tree is dirty |\n| `WS /ws/terminal?projectId=` | PTY bytes in/out, plus a `resize` message (Phase 3) |\n\nEvery git and terminal route takes a `projectId` and resolves the path from state —\n**never** a path supplied by the client. That is the one input-validation rule that\nreally matters here.\n\n---\n\n## UI\n\n```\n+------------+------------------------------+---------------------+\n| PROJECTS   |  CHAT                        |  CHANGES            |\n|            |                              |                     |\n| v Com8     |  +- chat: \"article schema\" -+|  M  src/app/page.tsx|\n|   Studio   |  |  ...streamed prose...    ||  M  lib/schema.ts   |\n|   |-article|  |  [+] Edit lib/schema.ts  ||  ?  docs/notes.md   |\n|   +-perf   |  |  [+] Bash npm run build  ||                     |\n| > Com8     |  +--------------------------+|  +- diff ----------+ |\n|   Sanity   |  [ prompt input           ] |  | +  ...          | |\n| + add      |  mode: acceptEdits v  [send] |  +----------------+ |\n|            |                              |  [stage] [commit]   |\n+------------+------------------------------+---------------------+\n                         [ terminal ]  <- Phase 3, collapsible drawer\n```\n\n- **Left** — projects, each expanding to its chats. `+ add` opens the folder picker\n  (starts at `E:\\muhaz\\CStudio`, browses anywhere).\n- **Middle** — the active chat. Prose streams inline; every tool call is a collapsible\n  card (`[+] Edit lib/schema.ts`) holding the diff or command output. Permission-mode\n  dropdown per chat: `acceptEdits` / `manual` / `bypassPermissions` / `plan`.\n- **Right** — SCM for the active project: file list, diff, stage, commit, stash, fetch,\n  pull.\n- **Bottom** — Phase 3 terminal drawer, a plain shell in the project folder.\n- A project with a live agent process shows a running indicator, so two chats don't\n  quietly edit the same tree at once.\n\n---\n\n## Phases\n\n**Phase 1 — talk to a project** (the only phase that must exist to be useful)\n\n- Add / list / remove projects, folder picker defaulting to `CStudio`\n- Create a chat, send a prompt, stream the response\n- Prose + collapsible tool cards\n- Per-chat permission mode, defaulting to `acceptEdits`\n- Abort a running chat; resume a chat by session id\n\n**Phase 2 — see and commit what changed**\n\n- `status` file list: staged / unstaged / untracked\n- Diff view (Monaco diff editor)\n- Stage / unstage / discard; commit with a message\n- Stash, stash pop\n- History replay when reopening a chat\n\n**Phase 3 — terminal and the rest of source control**\n\n- Plain shell per project (`node-pty` + `xterm.js` over WebSocket), collapsible drawer\n- Fetch, pull, branch list + guarded checkout, commit history\n- Sub-chats in the sidebar\n- Per-project `verifyCommand` with a one-click run and output panel\n- Per-project `CLAUDE.md` editor\n\n---\n\n## Risks and things to get right\n\n- **Child-process lifecycle.** Map `chatId -> ChildProcess`. Kill on abort, on chat\n  delete, and on server shutdown. An orphaned `claude` process holds a session and\n  keeps working invisibly.\n- **SSE plumbing.** Stream from Fastify with `Content-Type: text/event-stream` and no\n  compression on that route. Verify with a slow response *before* building UI on it.\n- **`node-pty` on Windows (Phase 3).** It installs from shipped prebuilds under plain\n  Node — no compiler needed. Two known sharp edges: kill a PTY whose console has\n  already exited and ConPTY's console-process enumeration can throw, and a browser\n  refresh must dispose the PTY or processes leak. Own both explicitly.\n- **Windows paths.** Backslashes in JSON, spaces in paths, `E:\\` vs `/e/` between Node\n  and any shell call. Always pass argv arrays, never a concatenated command string.\n- **Concurrent chats, one working tree.** Documented above; surface it in the UI rather\n  than trying to solve it.\n- **Long output.** Stream, don't buffer. Large diffs need virtualised lists or the\n  Changes tab will jank on a big refactor.\n\n---\n\n## Deferred (deliberately not in v1)\n\n- Multi-agent anything — no orchestrator, no agent-to-agent messaging, no roster.\n- Worktree isolation, per-agent branches.\n- Any remote access, tunnel, or phone control.\n- Scheduled or background runs. Nothing happens unless you press something.\n","numLines":298,"startLine":1,"totalLines":298}}}
